[[File:S2E50 Lord Casterwill children.png|thumb|170px|[[Lord Casterwill]] and his children seal the [[Spiral Mark]]]]
The Casterwill lineage began with [[Lord Casterwill]], the original and first [[Seeker]] who was responsible for bringing the [[Titans]] to Earth from the [[Spirit World]], Huntik. He forged the [[Amulets]] and [[Rings]] in order to anchor them to this dimension in order for them to battle the [[Nullifiers]], evil creatures of unimaginable power and destruction. {{Source|All Work and No Pay}} After a 500-year conflict, Casterwill finally freed Earth from the Nullifiers and peacefully died where he stood. {{Source|Coming of Age}} 

Before his death, Casterwill passed on the responsibility to his four children, sealing the [[Spiral Mark]] with the [[Willblade]], ensuring it could never be used again as a beacon to summon the Nullifiers. {{Source|The Spiral Mark}} However, Casterwill's best friend was a traitor, known only as [[the Betrayer]], who attempted to reopen the mark using [[Void]], the Nullifier scout. Casterwill's sons and daughters defeated him however, preventing the Nullifiers from returning. {{Source|Chasing Void}}

Without a common enemy, many Seekers turned to evil. The Casterwill family began to be hunted by the [[Blood Spiral]], a deadly group devoted to bringing back the Nullifiers and wiping out civilization. Many branches were completely wiped out and the remaining members of the family were forced to go into hiding. {{Source|The Blood Spiral}} Their locations were kept a secret at [[the Cloisters]] and guarded by [[Focauld Casterwill]], the keeper of knowledge. {{Source|The Casterwill Connection}}
[[File:S2E38 Kiel Sophie.png|thumb|170px|[[Sophie Casterwill]] faces [[Kiel]], the Spiral who killed her parents]]
After her parents were killed in fire caused by [[Kiel]] at the [[Paris Casterwill house]], [[Sophie Casterwill]] was rescued by [[Santiago]] and taken to a Casterwill safehouse where she was raised by [[LeBlanche]], the caretaker, before eventually moving to Venice for high school.  {{source|Sophie on Trial}} As an orphan, now cut from the other branch families, she thought herself to be the sole surviving member of the Casterwill lineage and believed she would never learn the secrets of her family. {{source|Memory Lane}} However, she later learnt that her brother, [[Lucas Casterwill]], had also survived but had gone into hiding. {{Source|Chasing Void}} After speaking to [[Eathon Lambert]] and seeing a vision of [[Lord Casterwill]] in the [[Crystal Caves]] that she discovered that she was, in fact, a direct descendant of the very first Casterwill. {{source|Cave of the Casterwills}}
[[File:S2E39 Fortress of Iron Will meeting.png|thumb|170px|Some of the Casterwill family gather in the [[Fortress of Iron Will]]]]
One Casterwill, [[Teien Casterwill|Teien]] took a position on the [[Huntik Foundation Council]], but kept her true identity a secret. {{Source|The Casterwill Connection}} She asked the Huntik team for help to activate the [[Blue Star]] to signal to the surviving members of the Casterwill family to come out of hiding and unite against the returning [[Blood Spiral Brotherhood|Blood Spiral]]. Following the quatrains on Eathon's Holotome, [[Lok Lambert]] managed to retrieve the [[Legendary Titan]] of Summons, [[Quetzalcoatl]] and successfully activate the signal. {{source|The Titan in the Temple of Sun}} However, only a fraction of the family came to the [[Fortress of Iron Will]] for the meeting of the Elders. {{source|Sophie on Trial}} After a huge battle against a Spiral Army, Sophie won leadership of the Casterwill family after succeeding in the Trial of Courage test to awaken and bond to [[Mythras]], the [[Legendary Titan]] of Bravery, defeating [[Kiel]] for good in the process. {{Source|The Spiral War}}

On the longest night of the year, members of the Casterwill family fought side by side with the [[Huntik Foundation]] at the [[Blood Spiral Base]], eventually defeating the Blood Spiral. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}} {{Source|Dante's Return}}

*The House of Nobles was led by the parents of [[Lucas]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] until they were murdered by [[Kiel]] through arson. Lucas became this House's new Elder.{{source|Sophie on Trial}}
*The House of Blade Makers was led by its Elder, [[Nimue Casterwill]], the Lady of the Lake, until her sacrifice to hold off the [[Blood Spirals]] who were trying to attack the [[Fortress of Iron Will]]. Afterwards, [[Vivian Casterwill]] inherited the leadership position. {{source|The Spiral War}}
*The House of Knowledge is led by its Elder, [[Focauld Casterwill]]. {{source|Sophie on Trial}}
*The House of Strategists is led by [[Teien Casterwill]]. {{source|Sophie on Trial}}
*The [[Elder Rue Guardian]] oversees his house and the curses that protect the secrets of the Casterwill family. {{source|Sophie on Trial}}
